    "title": "⛳ Final Round — A Message from Your Commissioner",
    "showFrom": "2026-04-12T07:00:00-04:00",
    "showUntil": "2026-04-12T14:00:00-04:00",
    "message": "<p>Gentlemen, it is Sunday at Augusta National.</p><p>On Friday, this pool looked like a foregone conclusion. A six shot lead. Historic. Inevitable. And then Augusta did what Augusta does — it reminded everyone that nothing here is settled until the last putt drops on 18.</p><p>As we begin the day, Caleb still leads the pool. Rory is still in it. But so is everyone else. Kade is in second. Blake and Keith are two back of Kade and very much alive. Josh and I are right there. Kyle continues to defy explanation. Even Matt's guy woke up on Saturday.</p><p>That is the Masters. That is why we are all watching today.</p><p>The green jacket will be awarded this afternoon. The draft order will be determined. Fortunes will be made and lost across three holes of Amen Corner, and there is nothing any of us can do about it except watch, refresh this page, and remind ourselves that this is exactly why we watch the Masters every year.</p><p>Taylor, for his part, has nothing to worry about today. His position is already locked in. Two consecutive last place finishes, and now a last place draft pick. The man has achieved a kind of serenity the rest of us can only aspire to.</p><p>Go watch golf, gentlemen. It's going to be a good one.</p><p>— BenGPT</p>"
  },
